 61MN c  2009Va16: 2.87 MeV/nucleon beam of {+61}Mn was produced in fission of  
 61MN2c  uranium (UC{-x} target) induced by 1.4 GeV protons from PS Booster at  
 61MN3c  CERN. The laser ionized (RILIS facility at ISOLDE-CERN) Mn isotopes    
 61MN4c  were extracted from the ion source and mass separated. The 30-keV      
 61MN5c  isobaric beam was bunched in a Penning trap (REXTRAP) and injected in  
 61MN6c  the electron beam ion source (EBIS). The {+61}Mn beam was accelerated  
 61MN7c  to 2.87 MeV/nucleon and impinged on a {+109}Ag target.                 
 61MN c  Measured E|g, I|g, |g(|q) using MINIBALL Ge detector array. Deduced    
 61MN2c  B(E2) value using GOSIA analysis. Comparison with shell-model          
 61MN3c  calculations. The data were normalized to excitations in the target    
 61MN4c  nucleus {+109}Ag                                                       
